{% doc %}
  @prompt
    Create a Shopify theme section that closely matches the provided reference image of a premium coffee brand’s journal/blog section. Reproduce the layout, spacing, typography, colors, card design, and overall visual appearance as accurately as possible.
    
    ### Section Layout
    - Use a warm cream background (#F7F3E9 or a very similar shade).
    - Add approximately 36px horizontal padding on desktop.
    - At the top, display a small uppercase eyebrow label: “FROM THE ROASTER'S JOURNAL” in dark green, bold, compact text.
    - Below it, add a large heading: “A little coffee know-how.” Use a clean, modern sans-serif font, dark forest green (#21483D), approximately 36px on desktop with regular font weight.
    - Add a short subtitle underneath: “Brewing tips, everyday rituals and stories worth sharing over a cup.” Use muted gray-green text around 15px.
    - Maintain the reference image’s generous whitespace and left alignment.
    
    ### Blog Cards Grid
    Create three equal-width blog cards in a single horizontal row on desktop, with approximately 20px gaps between cards.
    
    Each card should have:
    1. A large, edge-to-edge featured image at the top, approximately 172px tall on desktop.
    2. Slightly rounded top image corners, around 5px.
    3. A white-warm background (#FFFCF6) for the content area.
    4. A subtle light beige border (#E5E0D5) and a small border radius of 6px.
    5. Internal content padding of approximately 15px.
    
    Use these three example blog posts:
    
    **Card 1**
    - Category: “EVERYDAY RITUALS”
    - Title: “Make room for a slower morning.”
    - Description: “A little pause, a favorite mug and time for a good cup.”
    - Link: “Read story”
    - Image: A woman enjoying coffee in a green ceramic mug while sitting in a bright, sunlit outdoor lounge. Include a bag of premium coffee beside her.
    
    **Card 2**
    - Category: “NEIGHBORHOOD RITUALS”
    - Title: “Good coffee is better together.”
    - Description: “Small moments that bring a neighborhood a little closer.”
    - Link: “Read story”
    - Image: An older couple sitting outdoors in a garden, smiling and drinking coffee together, with a premium coffee bag between them.
    
    **Card 3**
    - Category: “BREW BETTER”
    - Title: “A better cup starts with the basics.”
    - Description: “Small details to bring a little more care to your daily brew.”
    - Link: “Read story”
    - Image: A man brewing pour-over coffee in a bright modern kitchen, with a kettle, dripper, coffee server, and premium coffee bag visible.
    
    ### Card Typography and Styling
    - Category labels: uppercase, dark green, approximately 9px, bold.
    - Card titles: dark forest green, approximately 21px, regular font weight, with compact line spacing.
    - Descriptions: muted gray-green (#77786D), approximately 12px, with a line height of 1.5.
    - Place the “Read story” link at the bottom left of each card in bold dark green text, approximately 11px.
    - Add a simple thin right-arrow icon at the bottom right of each card.
    - Use flexbox so the links and arrows align along the bottom edge of all three cards, even when titles or descriptions wrap onto different numbers of lines.
    - Make the entire card clickable, as well as its “Read story” link. Link each card to its corresponding Shopify blog article.
    
    ### Bottom CTA Button
    Below the three cards, align one button to the left with approximately 30px of top spacing.
    - Button text: “Explore the journal”
    - Add a right-arrow icon on the right side of the text.
    - Use a transparent or cream background.
    - Add a thin dark green border, approximately 1px.
    - Use a subtle 4px corner radius.
    - Use bold dark green text around 12px.
    - Apply approximately 12px vertical and 14px horizontal padding.
    - On hover, use a dark green background with white text and a smooth transition.
    - Make the button link to the main Shopify blog/journal page.
    
    ### Shopify Theme Editor Settings
    Make the section fully editable through the Shopify theme customizer. Include:
    - Eyebrow text
    - Main heading
    - Subtitle
    - Background and text colors
    - Card background, border, and text colors
    - Blog selection
    - Number of blog posts to display
    - Individual card images, with automatic featured-image fallback
    - Card categories, titles, descriptions, and article links
    - CTA button label and URL
    - Desktop and mobile spacing controls
    - Image height and card border-radius controls
    
    Use Shopify Liquid and schema settings so the section can be added, removed, and customized from the theme editor. If possible, support selecting a Shopify blog and automatically rendering its latest articles. Allow manual overrides for each card's image and category label.
    
    ### Responsive Design
    - Desktop: three cards in one row.
    - Tablet: two cards per row, with the third card wrapping onto the next row.
    - Mobile: stack all cards vertically in a single column.
    - Reduce horizontal padding on mobile to approximately 18px.
    - Scale the main heading to approximately 28px on mobile.
    - Keep card images full-width with a consistent aspect ratio.
